 "verdict": "no_edge",
 "conclusion": "CLEAN NEGATIVE on the swap hypothesis. Walk-forward pooled logistic regression on the established prob features is the SAME signal as the empirical-bin layer (per-date disc correlation 0.94-0.96) but nominally worse in all 4 horizon x liquidity cells (paired diff h10 -0.18pp t-0.20; h20 -0.65pp t-0.62; at h20/liq50 empirical +7.66 t3.08 vs logistic +5.28 t1.73). Raw logistic P is mildly mis-calibrated at the extremes (negative Brier skill) because the pooled-linear-logit functional form extrapolates beyond what the rank bins support; bin recalibration of the logistic score fixes level but not ranking. Adding surprise (sue/npq_yoy raw or as the final_model magnitude score) adds ZERO P(up) information conditional on vol/value, confirming P(up) and E[ret] are different targets. RECOMMENDATION: keep the empirical score-rank-bin layer (caliblib, target=rel) as the production calibration; do not adopt logistic."
}